NAME
    log - emit one localized structured runtime log record

SYNOPSIS
    log <severity> <domain> <message-id> [<field> <value>]...

DESCRIPTION
    log emits a structured record to standard error when the requested severity
    is enabled by m_LOG_LEVEL.

    Supported severities are:
        fatal error warn info debug trace

    Message text is resolved through the technical lang facility. Additional
    fields are supplied as name/value pairs and are appended to the record.

    m_LOG_LEVEL accepts the current filtering levels off/none, fatal, error,
    warn, info, debug and trace/all.

    Every operand is validated before filtering. A filtered record is silent
    only when the complete invocation is valid.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m log [arguments].


EXIT STATUS

    Bootstrap failures (before operation dispatch):
    1    m_ROOT is missing or empty; invoke the command through m or
         from an initialized m environment.
    2    The m shell runtime could not be loaded.
    Operation-specific failures below may also use these numeric
    statuses; stderr identifies the bootstrap or operation branch.

    0   Valid record emitted or filtered by m_LOG_LEVEL.
    1   Missing severity, domain or message identifier.
    2   Invalid severity.
    3   Invalid m_LOG_LEVEL.
    4   Invalid domain.
    5   Invalid message identifier.
    6   Field arguments are not name/value pairs.
    7   Invalid field name.

SEE ALSO
